db/id "q-181688" :question/id #uuid "99e67b20-b67b-5919-b8dd-1b6166de0f1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-181688" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063256/assets/4628a6e45445a585361f7d32586b27e29bc726d4ed8b7f072679e5537df59644.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x+1\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,3x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=x+1$ and *below* the line $y=3x.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>x+1,\\,y<3x.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\nx+1<y<3x.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=3x$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\nx+1<y\\le 3x\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+1<y\\le 3x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-181688/field-1" "q-181688/field-2" "q-181688/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181688"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181689/field-1/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf" :answer/id #uuid "7cf35a35-ef11-5c48-bc8c-b6379abf4dc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181689/field-1/62fc74d0eb6ece7bf9beb52d92d3e5dd4c591eb0e1df3eb95bec90a49e0fa322" :answer/id #uuid "9cf104c5-6f45-5b3c-8de8-09f6b7fc7252" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/v