g this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n3x<y<\\frac{x}{4}.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=3x$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n3x\\le y<\\frac{x}{4}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3x\\le y<\\frac{x}{4}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-181689/field-1" "q-181689/field-2" "q-181689/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181689"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-182013/field-1/a1f44d584f3d5c0539cb338e6289ad49d176231f52c1da87f334282351fe2472" :answer/id #uuid "14132d5c-0f1f-5785-bfda-ba8432592f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182013/field-1/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf" :answer/id #uuid "6ea44f6d-1c2f-5747-9d0b-9191fbd7c26a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182013/field-1/62fc74d0eb6ece7bf9beb52d92d3e5dd4c591eb0e1df3eb95bec90a49e0fa322" :answer/id #uuid "c592b6ab-4b76-544f-8b35-3a9e61b10209" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182013/field-1/5fc5100246d98d57a3a3e1d40181b00e6e8dff5d4a097ce2d7b7f6ae0b08578e" :answer/id #uuid "5119a61b-4d48-51c6-b91f-7e1d6c114c3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182013/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2e273a9-2135-5aa8-a51c-738cab0c46c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-182013/field-1/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d