d139011f0b8b63f9cad9aaf57f40ab2b8d40ee2eb" "q-182013/field-2/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19" "q-182013/field-2/55f4eef1ef55065220056c9644bf18d21761bc8db2d8f5c41f767a2fc9186b70" "q-182013/field-2/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-182013" :question/id #uuid "0ffa407b-8974-5c7d-bae0-120b5fa4ce86" :question/math-academy-id "q-182013" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063256/assets/7703b8c621b268a9fcbb412cd3a0617045145d475024dc91cecfa09a18fc8712.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,-2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *right* the line $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\nx>-2\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $x=-2$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\nx\\ge -2\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge -2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-182013/field-1" "q-182013/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e694b201-5ec6-5cc3-a608-2447d1cc1ed3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-182013"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
